title-1999-catalogue-raisonne"}},"type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Georgia O'Keeffe","id":"actor/2","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Birmingham Museum of Art","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"A bright green apple rests on a circular black plate. The background of the work is painted solid white.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"The Green Apple, 1922","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Museum purchase with funds provided by the 1981 and 1982 Museum Dinners and Balls, the Museum Store, Donors, and matching funds from Mr. and Mrs. Jack McSpadden, 1983.28","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on canvas","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"14 1/8 x 12 1/8 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Complete","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_complete"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe. The Green Apple, 1922. Oil on canvas, 14 1/8 x 12 1/8 inches. Birmingham Museum of Art. Museum purchase with funds provided by the 1981 and 1982 Museum Dinners and Balls, the Museum Store, Donors, and matching funds from Mr. and Mrs. Jack McSpadden, 1983.28. © Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe (1887-1986); purchased from O'Keeffe, through Alfred Stieglitz, New York, by Harold Greengard, New York, 1923; descended to his son, Frederick L. Grayson, 1972; purchased from Grayson, through Doris Bry, New York, by the Birmingham Museum of Art, Alabama, 1983 (Source: Birmingham Museum of Art, 2026)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Oil on canvas, 14 1/8 x 12 1/8 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Whitney Archive indicates, \"Painted 1921.\" Whitney Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks indicate, \"Sold to Harold Greengard. . . Green apple on black plate. See gallery photograph, 4–f.\" Abiquiú Notebooks after 1977 indicates, \"Purchased by Birmingham Museum of Art, 1981.\" Stretcher inscription 1 dates 1922 and illegible area would indicate number in 1923 New York (Anderson) exhibition. Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive date c. 1921. Abiquiú Notebooks dates 1921. Dated 1922 on basis of stretcher inscription 1. Pictured in 1923 New York (Anderson) Stieglitz installation photograph, see Appendix III, figure 15. Titled *Green Apple on Black Plate*, 1921? and that work was included in 1923 exhibition by O'Keeffe on Abiquiú Notebooks photograph; *The Green Apple Still Life* by O'Keeffe on 2nd Abiquiú Notebooks photograph; *Apple \u0026 Tray – Green \u0026 Black*, 1922 Stieglitz on 3rd Abiquiú Notebooks photograph; *The Green Apple*, 1921 by Stieglitz on 4th Abiquiú Notebooks photograph. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/872341/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/872341"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}